xnu 0187: a wedged CP must not take the CPU with it

Every boot that ended in a black panel and no ring ended the same way in the
log: the CP was started, Neo5seGPU was published, the first Mesa stream was
dumped -- and then nothing. The user client's diagnostics after a missed fence
read CP and SMMU registers, and a CP that has wedged stalls those reads, so the
CPU hangs inside one of them. The reset thread that writes the "boot-fastboot"
BCB never gets to run and the phone has to be power-cycled by hand.

Print the fence verdict from the fence word in memory, which needs no GPU
register and always can be said, and put the register reads (SQE_STAT, IB1/IB2,
fault statuses) behind gpudump=1. With a wedge now survivable the phone returns
to fastboot by itself, which is what makes an experiment loop possible.

